  "captions": {
    "s1_seed_rotation": "Twenty completed games, grouped by five seed blocks and four cyclic seat rotations. Cells report the winning configured agent, seat and game turns. Shared seeds do not produce identical opportunities; one observed trajectory occupies each cell. These are cohort outcomes, not an intrinsic model ranking.",
    "s2_spending_windows": "Each point is one game/player/color group with positive own house or hotel spending. Paid developed rent is shown after the first own expenditure; triangles contain an inherited deed at that point. Totals compare this window with whole-game receipts. The 450-dollar difference is pre-spending income from inherited G2 light blues. Paid rent excludes unpaid bankruptcy debts. Neither window is incremental return; inherited improvements, salvage, acquisition cost, timing and terminal censoring remain separate.",
    "s3_g19_dark_blue": "Observed receipts for two game/player/dark-blue spending units on the same deeds in G19. Squares mark observed complete-ownership boundaries; dotted lines mark first own spending. Lines stop at each unit's last paid-rent event, not at the end of ownership. Panels share scales and retain different owners, inherited routes and spending/sale histories. Event order is not time at risk. This contrast does not identify an owner effect, a return caused by construction, or a counterfactual investment outcome."
  },
